---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [["Does pct= affect aggregate reports?", "No. Reports are generated for all messages regardless of pct=. The tag only controls the enforcement action."], ["Can I use pct= with p=none?", "There is no effect. p=none already delivers all mail regardless of pct=."]];

const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: "DMARC pct Tag",
  description: "DMARC pct= tag explained: gradual policy rollout with percentage-based enforcement. pct=25, pct=50, pct=100.",
  inLanguage: 'en',
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
  publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PromptDNS', url: 'https://promptdns.com/', logo: { '@type': 'ImageObject', url: 'https://promptdns.com/favicon.svg' } },
  datePublished: '2026-10-27',
  dateModified: '2026-10-27',
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};

const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://promptdns.com/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Email Authentication', item: 'https://promptdns.com/email-authentication/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "DMARC pct Tag" },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DMARC pct Tag: Gradual Policy Rollout with Percentage-Based Enforcement"
  description="DMARC pct= tag explained: gradual policy rollout with percentage-based enforcement. pct=25, pct=50, pct=100."
  schema={[article, faqSchema, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DMARC pct Tag</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DMARC pct Tag</h1>
    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg text-ink-dim">DMARC pct= tag explained: gradual policy rollout with percentage-based enforcement. pct=25, 50, 100.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="not-prose my-8" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class='pdns-table' style='width:100%'><thead><tr><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>pct= value</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Effect with p=quarantine</th><th class='whitespace-nowrap'>Effect with p=reject</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='pd-mono'>100 (default)</td><td>All failing mail goes to spam</td><td>All failing mail is bounced</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>50</td><td>50% of failing mail to spam, 50% delivered</td><td>50% bounced, 50% delivered</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>25</td><td>25% to spam, 75% delivered</td><td>25% bounced, 75% delivered</td></tr><tr><td class='pd-mono'>0</td><td>No policy applied (same as p=none)</td><td>No policy applied (same as p=none)</td></tr></tbody></table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <article class="rich-text mt-10 max-w-none">
      <h2>Technical details</h2>
      <p class='mt-3'>The DMARC pct= tag controls the percentage of failing messages that receive the policy specified by p=, enabling gradual rollout of enforcement without affecting all failing mail simultaneously.</p><p class='mt-3'>The default value is 100, meaning all failing messages receive the policy. Setting pct=25 means only 25% of failing messages are quarantined or rejected while the remaining 75% are delivered normally.</p><p class='mt-3'>The pct= tag only applies when p= is quarantine or reject; it has no effect when p=none because no policy action is taken on failing messages.</p>

      <aside class="mt-8 rounded-xl border-l-3 border-l-violet/50 bg-violet/5 p-5" aria-label="Practitioner field notes">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-violet mb-2">Field notes</p>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim italic">The pct= tag is your safety net during enforcement rollout. Start at pct=25, watch aggregate reports for a week, then increase to 50, 75, and finally 100. If legitimate mail starts failing, reduce pct= immediately instead of reverting p=.</p>
      </aside>

      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
        <details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does pct= affect aggregate reports?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No. Reports are generated for all messages regardless of pct=. The tag only controls the enforcement action.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can I use pct= with p=none?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">There is no effect. p=none already delivers all mail regardless of pct=.</p></details>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        Check your domain with our free tools:
        <a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SPF checker</a>,
        <a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DMARC checker</a>,
        <a href="/dkim-record-checker/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DKIM checker</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
